{
  "description": "The audio topology of a resident speech session's open, as the host asks for it and as the engine confirms it. Frozen with the voice platform on 2026-09-18: the existing open and the existing audio object, with NO INPUT spelled as audio.input PRESENT and null and no input_handle at all. No input is not an empty input and not a finished one; omission is never read as absence. The PCM encoding is s16le: audio.format may be omitted (s16le is meant) and any other value — another encoding, null, a non-string — is refused, never read as s16le. Entries marked canonical are the exact open a host sends. The runtime owns this file (spec/audio/vectors); the kit carries a byte-for-byte copy.",
